        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: સંભવતઃ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સંભવતઃ — sambhavataḥ — \"probably\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો ટ્રેન સમયસર હશે તો અમે સંભવતઃ સાંજે પહોંચીશું. jo ṭren samaysar haśe to ame sambhavataḥ sā̃je pahõcīśũ. If the train is on time, we will probably arrive by evening."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સંભવતઃ (sambhavataḥ) is built from Sanskrit sambhava, \"coming about, possibility\" (Monier-Williams), and the adverb ending -taḥ: by way of what is possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
